# Rung-2 close smoke (2026-08-01). TWO legs, ~300-500k.
#
# Same two legs as the cycle-7 pre-pair smoke (smoke7_20260730_104806), so the
# "zero verdict changes" criterion has a real baseline instead of an assumption:
#   Closure-62_c -> TN in smoke7
#   Math-65_c    -> FP in smoke7
# Math-65_c is also the archive's richest repair leg (8 rejections, 6 cleared,
# both shipped repair types), so the repair marker has something to mark.
#
# WHAT THIS SMOKE MUST SHOW (rung-2 gate, all four):
#   1. mislabel refusal   — tested separately and offline (8.8 exits 2 on a
#                           -c/Doverfitting mismatch); NOT exercised here,
#                           because a deliberately broken cases file would
#                           refuse to launch and produce no run.
#   2. repair marker      — an ACCEPTED harness carrying
#                           "[FROM REPAIRED ATTEMPT: ...]" and its detail fields
#                           (8.7). This is the first LIVE exercise of that field.
#   3. five rate states   — the 8.13 split observed in a real trace, not a test:
#                           no-measurement / buggy-side-unmeasured / below-bar /
#                           catch-profile-skipped / at-or-above-bar. Some states
#                           are rare, so the gate is "every state that appears is
#                           one of the five, and at least two distinct appear".
#   4. zero verdict changes vs smoke7 on these two legs.
#
# Rung 2 is protective code with no verdict surface: 8.7 adds a trace field, 8.8
# refuses bad input, 8.12(a) is tests only. If a verdict moves, something
# unintended changed and the batch does not close.
#
# Config matches the pair and the cycle-7 smoke exactly (-n 5 -m 12).
MODEL="gpt-5.4"
COMMON="-n 5 -m 12 --fuzz_timeout 20 --verify_timeout 20 --verify_relations --synthesize_relations --replay_relations_on_patched --rule_compile_repair"
CASES=(
  "-c patchfile:/home/code/drr/Patches/Dcorrect/Jaid/Closure/patch1-Closure-62-Jaid.patch"
  "-c patchfile:/home/code/drr/Patches/Dcorrect/CapGen/Math/patch1-Math-65-CapGen.patch"
)
